organize (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the command from organize-dl to organize. organize-dl stays as a
    deprecated wrapper that forwards its arguments and turns --dry-run into
    --preview.
  * Default to the current directory instead of ~/Downloads.
  * Add --preview, which replaces --dry-run.
  * Add --images, --documents, --music, --videos, --archives and --others to
    restrict a run to one or more categories.
  * Refuse system directories and the root of a git repository with exit 4.
  * Skip files that a download manager is still writing.
  * The package is now named organize and replaces organize-dl.

 -- Ivanadrian31 <ivanadrian31@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0700

